rust-proxmox-network-api (1.0.8-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * convert carriage returns in interface comments to newlines when writing the
    network configuration. ifupdown2 reads a standalone carriage return as a
    line break, which allowed injecting configuration lines through a comment.

  * reject interface comments containing the '${' or '<%' template tags, and
    export the comment schemas for API users. If python3-mako is installed,
    ifupdown2 renders the interfaces file as a template, which would execute
    such tags as Python code.

 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:58:28 +0100

rust-proxmox-network-api (1.0.7-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * move the Linux bond mode and transmit hash policy types to
    proxmox-network-types and re-export them, so existing users keep working
    unchanged.

 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:06:38 +0200

rust-proxmox-network-api (1.0.6-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * fix #7329: interfaces: support the IPv6 auto method, so listing interfaces
    no longer fails when the network configuration uses it. The method is only
    accepted for IPv6.

  * interfaces: preserve dhcp, auto, and loopback methods on unrelated updates
    instead of changing them to manual and potentially dropping IPv6 settings.
    Use manual for static configurations without an address or gateway.

  * interfaces: reject a method other than static while an address or gateway
    is set for that address family, instead of silently keeping it static.

 -- Proxmox Support Team <support@proxmox.com>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:14:31 +0200

rust-proxmox-network-api (1.0.5-1) trixie; urgency=medium

